  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We can now read the data from the CSV file `u.data` into a Pandas [data frame](https://medium.com/r/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fpandas.pydata.org%2Fpandas-docs%2Fstable%2Freference%2Fapi%2Fpandas.DataFrame.html), and create a FastAI [data bunch](https://medium.com/r/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fdocs.fast.ai%2Fbasic_data.html%23Get-your-data-ready-for-training) which:1. Converts the Pandas data frame into tensors2. It splits the data into a training set and a validation set3. Creates data loaders to access the data in batches4. Checks if a GPU is available, and moves the data to the GPU"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "In just 15 seconds, the mean squared error has come down to around 0.82, which is quite close to the state of the art (as compared with [these benchmarks](https://medium.com/r/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.librec.net%2Frelease%2Fv1.3%2Fexample.html)). And it only took us 8 lines of code to load the data and train the model!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
